WEBVTT

00:25.741 --> 00:30.078
FOOL NIGHT

01:42.025 --> 01:42.984
TRANSFLORA MEDICAL

01:43.068 --> 01:44.402
Your policies are inhumane!

01:44.486 --> 01:46.738
Reduce oxygen tax!

01:52.536 --> 01:54.871
Come on! We were only protesting!

01:54.955 --> 01:56.706
That's enough, you damn cops!

01:56.790 --> 02:00.377
Let us out already!
How long are you going to keep us here?

02:00.460 --> 02:02.671
There's a mandatory exit fee.

02:02.754 --> 02:06.508
Your only way out
is to pay bail of 1.2 million yen,

02:06.591 --> 02:09.928
a fine of 400,000 yen, and 200,000 yen
in damages to the riot police.

02:10.011 --> 02:13.390
We can't afford that!
That's why we're protesting!

02:13.473 --> 02:15.559
So what? Are we going to jail?

02:16.059 --> 02:21.398
I don't wanna go to jail…
I don't wanna go to jail…

02:21.481 --> 02:24.192
You people can't even go to jail.

02:25.068 --> 02:28.071
If you have no money,
Paupertown is your only option.

02:29.781 --> 02:32.701
- Paupertown?
- That's bullshit!

02:32.784 --> 02:37.330
You're just gonna bleed us dry
and throw us away? We won't survive!

02:37.414 --> 02:39.749
Dad? Hey, Dad…

02:39.833 --> 02:42.169
What's going to happen to us?

02:42.752 --> 02:44.921
Talk to me, Dad!

03:34.679 --> 03:36.681
<i>This is where Ivy…</i>

03:39.059 --> 03:40.101
<i>But as for me…</i>

03:45.023 --> 03:46.733
<i>What did I come here for?</i>

04:38.159 --> 04:42.122
Paupertown is for people
who can't live in the city anymore.

04:42.205 --> 04:44.833
They huddle together
in these old residences.

04:44.916 --> 04:46.501
It's similar to a slum.

04:54.509 --> 04:57.887
Unlike the city,
there's no underground heating here.

04:58.513 --> 05:01.182
Snow from 100 years ago
still hasn't melted.

05:01.933 --> 05:04.311
But the air is fresh here.

05:12.152 --> 05:15.071
The reason transfloration patients
are rarely seen in the city center

05:15.655 --> 05:19.117
is because most Spiriflora
are brought in from Paupertown.

05:19.951 --> 05:22.746
After complete transfloration,
they're brought back in.

05:23.705 --> 05:25.749
Isn't that twice the work?

05:25.832 --> 05:27.125
It's for aesthetics.

05:28.043 --> 05:31.087
Late-stage transfloration
is strongly associated with death.

05:31.963 --> 05:34.507
Staring at this all day
would be depressing.

05:44.851 --> 05:47.687
What's going on? Are we safe here?

05:48.396 --> 05:49.731
The parade is starting.

06:39.155 --> 06:42.575
About 15,000 people
reside here in Paupertown.

06:43.368 --> 06:47.163
They have minimal heating
and just enough food to survive.

06:47.247 --> 06:49.415
Their transfloration subsidies pay for it.

06:50.083 --> 06:54.045
The subsidies earned by a select few
are divided among all households here

06:54.129 --> 06:56.256
to cover their living expenses.

06:56.339 --> 07:01.052
Every year, about 100 of them
sell their lives to Transflora Medical.

07:02.512 --> 07:04.764
The Parade you wanted to see…

07:07.392 --> 07:09.310
is a shipment of sacrifices.

07:30.790 --> 07:32.500
But it's the 24th century…

07:33.209 --> 07:34.210
That's irrelevant.

07:34.919 --> 07:37.380
Why are they selecting children?6

07:38.173 --> 07:40.842
There are tons of adults
and old people to pick from…

07:41.885 --> 07:44.012
Didn't you read the reports?

07:44.888 --> 07:47.390
It's about their value
as human-sourced furniture.

07:48.141 --> 07:51.769
When elders undergo transfloration,
they produce less wood.

07:52.645 --> 07:56.149
Conversely, kids their age
grow into larger Spiriflora.

07:56.816 --> 07:58.735
Properly grown and sold,

07:58.818 --> 08:01.321
they can be worth
close to ten million yen.

08:05.783 --> 08:08.161
Did Yomiko know about this?

08:10.371 --> 08:11.498
Did she know?

08:11.581 --> 08:13.416
When she transflorated
Ivy's little sister?

08:20.507 --> 08:23.593
Normal employees know about it.
I'm positive they told her.

08:29.307 --> 08:31.643
Yesterday, you were thirsty for revenge.

08:31.726 --> 08:33.478
And today you're in despair?

08:34.270 --> 08:36.022
Blame Horai all you want,

08:36.105 --> 08:37.899
but working at Transflora Medical

08:37.982 --> 08:39.734
makes you equally as responsible.

08:42.237 --> 08:43.404
Same goes for me.

08:47.742 --> 08:50.286
Did you just say, "Ivy's little sister"?

08:52.539 --> 08:54.457
You spoke with Ivy, didn't you?

08:55.625 --> 08:58.711
Tell me what happened
and what you're capable of.

08:59.879 --> 09:02.090
If Ivy was born in Paupertown,

09:02.173 --> 09:04.425
that should give us some sort of hint.

09:05.009 --> 09:09.556
Then, we can solve Ivy's mystery
and bring back some answers.

09:14.394 --> 09:16.020
If we learn the truth,

09:16.104 --> 09:17.689
we can explain to the protestors.

09:17.772 --> 09:19.774
I won't force you to tell me, but…

09:22.694 --> 09:24.153
Answer me, you piece of shit!

09:26.114 --> 09:27.031
Fine.

09:27.115 --> 09:30.159
I'll be over there…

09:30.243 --> 09:31.286
Sorry.

09:31.369 --> 09:33.037
No worries.

09:33.121 --> 09:35.665
There are many things
we're better off not knowing.

09:35.748 --> 09:37.625
Chat quietly, okay?

09:39.752 --> 09:40.753
Go on.

09:45.508 --> 09:48.052
Three months ago,
I underwent transfloration.

09:49.012 --> 09:51.639
<i>After that, I started hearing Spiriflora.</i>

09:55.685 --> 09:58.938
Young Master, over here. Stay close, okay?

10:02.150 --> 10:03.610
Where are we goin'?

10:04.193 --> 10:06.946
To meet with Paupertown's big shot.

10:07.030 --> 10:11.242
He might lead us to a plantation owner
with information about Shiika Izumi.

10:12.285 --> 10:13.536
Plantation owner?

10:22.503 --> 10:24.422
Sorry to interrupt your meal.

10:24.505 --> 10:27.300
I have an inquiry
about human-sourced furniture.

10:28.801 --> 10:30.136
Where'd you come from?

10:30.720 --> 10:32.055
We're from Transflora Medical.

10:33.222 --> 10:34.766
Don't be so tense.

10:34.849 --> 10:36.601
I didn't come here to expose you.

10:40.063 --> 10:41.147
What do you want?

10:41.230 --> 10:43.858
An exclusive contract
with a certain plantation owner.

10:44.859 --> 10:48.363
I bought a beautifully crafted wardrobe
with cabriole legs the other day.

10:49.030 --> 10:51.282
It's made from
a magnificent single slab of wood,

10:51.366 --> 10:52.867
with a splendid natural grain.

10:53.451 --> 10:56.871
I heard that the Spiriflor
came from a plantation near here,

10:57.497 --> 10:59.999
so I'd like to reserve one for myself.

11:01.918 --> 11:03.544
Show me where it is, yeah?

11:08.966 --> 11:10.677
The plantation is just ahead.

11:12.011 --> 11:13.596
Hide your eyes if you have to.

11:38.037 --> 11:39.205
I'm gonna be sick.

11:41.290 --> 11:44.085
The children chosen for the parade

11:44.168 --> 11:46.337
are raised in this plantation,

11:46.421 --> 11:48.464
where they are shaped into workable timber

11:48.548 --> 11:51.342
once their transfloration
reaches a certain stage.

11:54.887 --> 11:59.225
After harvesting, the stump is left behind
to serve as a grave marker.

12:02.228 --> 12:05.106
Hey. That's the plantation owner's house.

12:14.949 --> 12:16.909
<i>Everything is made of wood…</i>

12:16.993 --> 12:18.077
Pleasure to meet you.

12:18.786 --> 12:22.665
I'm quite fond of the furniture
crafted from Spiriflora here.

12:23.332 --> 12:27.503
So I decided to visit this plantation
in hopes of reserving one for myself.

12:42.059 --> 12:43.811
Write your name on the list.

12:43.895 --> 12:45.354
It's a two-year wait.

12:51.903 --> 12:55.907
By the way, I was viewing a collection
at an acquaintance's house recently

12:56.824 --> 12:59.243
and noticed a particularly lovely piece.

13:00.036 --> 13:02.830
It was made from
a girl named Shiika Izumi.

13:02.914 --> 13:06.250
I'm awfully curious about how she grew up

13:06.334 --> 13:08.294
during her lifetime.

13:08.377 --> 13:10.129
Would you happen to know anything?

13:13.883 --> 13:17.428
Look up page 156 in that notebook.

13:17.512 --> 13:18.971
SHIIKA IZUMI

13:26.479 --> 13:27.438
Thanks.

13:31.651 --> 13:32.818
SHIIKA

13:32.902 --> 13:35.071
Ivy left an offering.

13:36.489 --> 13:37.615
This is awful.

13:39.158 --> 13:42.828
Hey, can't we do something
to save these kids?

13:42.912 --> 13:44.497
You've got influence, don't you?

13:44.580 --> 13:48.459
So you're saying you want me to expose
the human-sourced furniture industry

13:49.293 --> 13:51.504
and take away the residents' income?

13:52.588 --> 13:54.090
They'd starve to death.

13:59.929 --> 14:01.013
This is too cruel…

14:07.937 --> 14:09.814
Listen carefully. Here's the hard truth.

14:09.897 --> 14:11.732
This is fundamentally the same

14:11.816 --> 14:13.609
as the transfloration policy,

14:13.693 --> 14:14.860
just on a different scale.

14:14.944 --> 14:16.654
It's the so-called "trolley problem."

14:17.572 --> 14:19.615
<i>We bribe people to undergo transfloration</i>

14:19.699 --> 14:22.118
<i>and make a few sacrifices to get oxygen.</i>

14:22.201 --> 14:24.203
<i>That way, everyone else can breathe.</i>

14:25.162 --> 14:27.290
<i>The concept is no different.</i>

14:27.373 --> 14:29.542
<i>It's just the oxygen we can't see.</i>

14:30.209 --> 14:32.420
This is what transfloration entails.

14:34.422 --> 14:37.842
Securing maximum well-being
for as many people as possible.

14:37.925 --> 14:39.886
We work for a greater cause.

14:39.969 --> 14:43.472
You're one of the lucky majority
born on the other side.

14:45.516 --> 14:48.352
Make money. Grow up. Spike those numbers.

14:49.228 --> 14:51.314
Otherwise, you'll end up down here.

14:52.023 --> 14:56.944
DROP DEAD

15:06.996 --> 15:08.372
SHIIKA IZUMI
12-20 TOWER B, 603

15:39.362 --> 15:41.572
What's wrong? Hey, are you okay?

15:43.366 --> 15:44.367
I'm fine.

15:45.076 --> 15:47.620
I just feel a little dizzy.

15:49.497 --> 15:52.458
Close your eyes and face this way, please.

15:55.336 --> 15:56.837
Does that feel better?

15:56.921 --> 15:59.173
It's like being in a bright room, right?

16:06.013 --> 16:07.139
Thanks.

16:15.064 --> 16:17.316
MUKURU & SHIIKA IZUMI

16:17.900 --> 16:19.318
<i>"Mukuru Izumi."</i>

16:20.027 --> 16:21.487
<i>That's Ivy's real name.</i>

16:47.513 --> 16:49.890
<i>This is where Ivy…</i>

17:12.997 --> 17:15.708
What'cha doin'?
Are your Ivy senses tingling?

17:15.791 --> 17:17.543
Lemme guess, Toshiro.

17:17.626 --> 17:19.086
Are you a psychometrist?

17:19.170 --> 17:21.630
Well… Yeah, kinda.

17:22.506 --> 17:24.258
Do your thing.

17:29.096 --> 17:30.389
Adorbs.

17:30.973 --> 17:32.600
They're candy wrappers.

17:33.476 --> 17:36.771
There are records of Ivy
stealing candy from the victims, but…

17:40.816 --> 17:42.109
These are quite old.

17:43.069 --> 17:48.074
I'm guessing either Ivy or Shiika Izumi
found these while rummaging through trash.

17:54.080 --> 17:55.164
That's blood.

17:56.999 --> 17:58.334
We'll bring these sheets back.

18:06.008 --> 18:09.303
It's a sasanqua petal.
Looks like it's dried out.

18:10.221 --> 18:13.099
Wasn't Ivy an <i>Uncaria rhynchophylla?</i>

18:13.808 --> 18:19.021
Maybe someone hosting a sasanqua seed
moved in after Ivy left.

18:23.109 --> 18:23.943
Well?

18:25.361 --> 18:26.195
Quiet.

18:26.278 --> 18:27.696
HIKA, OTSA, SAKEN, KUDAI, RO

18:27.780 --> 18:30.032
It's… It's saying something.

18:30.116 --> 18:31.992
The song from that Parade earlier?

18:33.369 --> 18:36.956
"Hika, Otsa, Saken."

18:37.039 --> 18:41.043
"Kudai, Ro… Kudai, O…"

18:42.628 --> 18:43.712
Otaro Kudai?

18:44.839 --> 18:48.050
So does that mean
the other person is Ken Hikasa?

18:48.634 --> 18:50.553
Who are they? Do you know those guys?

18:51.345 --> 18:56.142
Otaro Kudai is one of three researchers
who invented transfloration.

18:56.225 --> 18:59.562
Ken Hikasa is one of the leaders
of the anti-transfloration movement.

19:00.479 --> 19:03.357
The fact that both their names
came up in this room means…

19:10.156 --> 19:13.200
They created Ivy right here in this room!

19:13.993 --> 19:17.454
The anti-transfloration movement,
with the help of a genius scientist!

19:18.414 --> 19:20.583
Unbelievable. I get it now…

19:21.292 --> 19:23.669
I totally underestimated the opposition.

19:25.296 --> 19:28.507
Wait, why would the opposition
transflorate somebody?

19:29.633 --> 19:31.760
Their objective wasn't to make Ivy.

19:32.511 --> 19:37.057
They wanted Ivy's massacre
to spark large-scale protests.

19:37.141 --> 19:38.893
That was their goal all along.

19:38.976 --> 19:43.189
They're trying to tarnish
the public image of transfloration

19:43.272 --> 19:46.442
to shrink or abolish the policy
by any means necessary.

19:47.151 --> 19:48.777
That's their ultimate goal.

19:50.863 --> 19:53.532
And I'm the one who pulled the trigger!

20:02.041 --> 20:03.125
<i>He's furious…</i>

20:04.627 --> 20:06.212
I get it now.

20:06.295 --> 20:09.715
They never told the public
about Ivy killing an opposition leader

20:10.382 --> 20:13.594
because they didn't want
incomplete data released until now.

20:14.428 --> 20:15.930
That's also how Ivy,

20:16.013 --> 20:19.308
who can't even speak,
stole a desk from Hiyama's hidden room.

20:19.391 --> 20:20.726
There was an accomplice.

20:22.728 --> 20:25.356
Damn it! I'm such an idiot!

20:28.108 --> 20:30.069
Where are those two guys now?

20:30.986 --> 20:35.532
Dr. Kudai has been missing for ages,
and some even say he's dead.

20:36.450 --> 20:39.745
Ken Hikasa should be reachable
through normal means of contact.

20:40.955 --> 20:42.164
All right, then.

20:43.332 --> 20:44.917
We need to find Ken Hikasa.

20:50.923 --> 20:53.175
That was productive, yeah?

20:53.259 --> 20:54.635
It's a good thing we came.

20:54.718 --> 20:55.636
Yeah.

20:55.719 --> 20:59.556
If we can prove that the opposition
is responsible for creating Ivy,

20:59.640 --> 21:01.392
we can protect Transflora Medical.

23:45.639 --> 23:50.644
Subtitle translation by: Logan Lampkins
